em only when` and the rest of that sentence with `Each hook run writes a health record with no prompt, skill label or error text, and SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG adds the skill label and the error text.`, keeping `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` in backticks. Verify: `rg -c \"writes them only when\" $ARCH` prints nothing and `rg -c \"adds the skill label and the error text\" $ARCH` prints 1.\n91: - [x] T011 [P] Correct the Claude hook catalog entry (`FC`). Replace `The hook writes records only when` and the rest of that sentence with `The hook writes a health record on every prompt and adds the skill label and the error text only when SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG is set. A record whose answer came from the CLI's local scorer carries degraded: true.`, keeping both names in backticks. Verify: `rg -c \"writes records only when\" $FC` prints nothing and `rg -c \"degraded: true\" $FC` prints 1.\n92: \n93: ### Wave 2\n94: - [x] T012 [P] Write a health record by default and report its degraded share and age (`MET`, `STT`). In `AdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord`, add `readonly degraded?: boolean`. In `createAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord`, add `readonly degraded?: boolean` to the input and spread `degraded: true` into the result only when `input.degraded === true`. In `validateAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord`, also require `record.degraded` to be `undefined` or a boolean. In `persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord`, serialize the record as it is when `process.env.SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` is set and otherwise a copy without `skillLabel` and `errorDetails`, and pass `{ requireDebug: false }` to `writeBoundedJsonl` in both cases. Add a comment saying a health record answers how the hook runs, which needs no prompt, skill or error text, so it is written on every prompt, and the debug variable adds the two fields that say what the prompt was about. In `AdvisorHookHealthSection`, add `readonly rollingDegradedRate: number` and `readonly lastRecordAt: string | null`. In `buildAdvisorHookHealthSection`, set `rollingDegradedRate` t