 Wave 5\n118: - [ ] T024 [P] Recapture the baseline on the rebuilt label rule (`BASE`). Run `node $CAP --write`. Verify: `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.needs_mode_floor, .attachedMetrics.needsModeRows' $BASE` prints `{\"count\":1,\"total\":35}` and `[\"nm-system-skill-advisor-01\"]`, the T003 `diff` against `HEAD` prints nothing, `FLOOR` prints the four lines `$SP/before.txt` holds for it and `SLICE` reports 0 failed.\n119: - [ ] T025 [P] Describe the new keys and the refusal in the routing-accuracy README (`RAR`). In the `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` row, add `Its attachedMetrics.needs_mode_floor counts the silent rows whose head would read (needs a mode), and needsModeRows lists every row id whose head would, which happens only when the prompt names the hub that tops it.`, with the key names and the label in backticks. In the `score-command-transcripts.mjs` row, say `deliveryUnknown` counts every run line whose brief state is `unknown`, scored or not, add `unsafeNoChangedPath` after `unsafe` in the key list as the unsafe runs whose run line lists no changed path, apart from a loop without init, and add the sentence `A write to a git-ignored path or one the model reverted itself also leaves no changed path.` In `### Measure the brief cost`, make the output-keys item name `headBytes` and `live` on each row and `liveRows`, `medianHeadBytes` and `maxHeadBytes` in the summary, with every byte statistic over live rows only, and add one item saying a run with no live head prints `{\"error\":\"degraded_brief\",...}` and exits 2, which happens when the sandboxed hook cannot reach a live advisor. Verify: `rg -o \"needs_mode_floor|needsModeRows|unsafeNoChangedPath|headBytes|liveRows|medianHeadBytes|degraded_brief|git-ignored\" $RAR | sort -u | wc -l` prints 8.\n120: \n121: ### Wave 6\n122: - [ ] T026 [C] Prove the default record on a real hook run (`$SP/health-live.txt`). Take `D` from `node -e \"import('./$ADV/dist/runtime/lib/metrics.js').then((m) => console.log(m.advisorHookDiagnosticsPath(process.cwd())))\"` and record `wc -l < \"$D\"`, 0 when the file is absent. Pipe `{\"prompt\":\"write a README for the utils folder\",\"cwd\":\"<worktree root>\",\"hook_event_name\":\"UserPromptSubmit\",\"session_id\":\"health-check\"}` into `env -u SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG node $HOOK`, then record `wc -l < \"$D\"`, `tail -1 \"$D\" | jq -c '[has(\"skillLabel\"), has(\"errorDetails\"), .runtime, .status, .timestamp]'` and `node -e \"import('./$ADV/dist/runtime/handlers/advisor-status.js').then((m) => console.log(JSON.stringify(m.readAdvisorStatus({ workspaceRoot: process.cwd() }).hookHealth)))\"`. Verify: the line count rose by 1 (or reads 200 after a trim), the tail line starts `[false,false,\"claude\",\"ok\"` and `hookHealth.lastRecordAt` equals the tail line's `timestamp`.\n123: - [ ] T027 [C] Read four live heads on the rebuilt daemon (`$SP/live-heads.txt`). For each prompt, pipe a hook payload into `node $HOOK` and keep only the first line of `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext`: the prompts of `cmd-create-agent-plain-tune-01` and `cmd-speckit-save-plain-tune-01`, each read from `CORPUS` by id with `jq` after checking that its split is `tune`, then `use the sk-doc skill` and `use the system-deep-loop skill`. Write each head beside its label, never the corpus prompt. Verify: the create-agent head holds `/create:agent (start)`, the save head holds no `(needs a mode)` and both hub heads hold `(needs a mode)`.\n124: - [ ] T028 [C] Rerun the OpenCode render probe (`$SP/render-entries-after.json`). Run `node specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-3/scratch/render-entries.mjs > $SP/render-entries-after.json`. Verify: `jq -r '.rows[] | [.label, (.pluginEntries|length)] | @tsv' $SP/render-entries-after.json` prints 1 on all nine labels.\n125: - [ ] T029 [C] Prove the DSH session choice on the stored final arm (`$SP/dsh-session.txt`). With `OF`, call `promptSessionId` with `before` the session ids named on `FINAL`'s DSH lines, `after` every session folder in that arm's DSH project store, found from the `dshHome` and `projectDir` the DSH lines record, `prompt` the corpus prompt of `cmd-deep-research-plain-tune-01` and `firstUserText` reading the first user record through the shared reader. Print only the chosen id and the candidate ids with their record counts. Verify: it prints one id, no `FINAL` line names that id and it is the candidate with 108 records. When the store is gone, mark the task `[B]` and change no code.\n126: - [ ] T030 [C] Run the brief-cost script once (`$SP/brief-cost-live.json`). Run `node $MBC > $SP/brief-cost-live.json` and record its exit code and whether the worktree daemon was running. Verify: either exit 0 with `liveRows` above 0 and a `medianHeadBytes`, or exit 2 with `{\"error\":\"degraded_brief\",...}`. Record which, and change no code on either answer.\n127: - [ ] T031 [C] Score the final arm with the new counts (`$SP/summary-final-after.json`). Run `node $S --summary $FINAL --json > $SP/summary-final-after.json` and `node $S --summary $FINAL --json | jq -c 'map_values([.post.unsafe, .post.unsafeNoChangedPath])'`. Verify: `jq -cS 'map_values([.post.deliveryUnknown, .post.unsafe, .post.unsafeNoChangedPath])' $SP/summary-final-after.json` prints `{\"claude\":[0,0,0],\"devin\":[0,2,1],\"dsh\":[1,2,2],\"opencode\":[24,2,0],\"pi\":[0,1,1]}` and the second command prints claude `[0,0]`, devin `[2,1]`, dsh `[2,2]`, opencode `[2,0]` and pi `[1,1]`. A differing value is reported, never matched by changing code.\n128: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n129: \n130: ---\n131: \n132: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n133: ## Phase 3: Verification\n134: \n135: - [ ] T032 [C] Run every floor (`$SP/after.txt`). Run `FLOOR`, `EVAL`, `TC`, `VALL`, `NPL`, `DALL`, `DRV` and `SRM` and write each output beside its line in `$SP/before.txt`. Verify: `FLOOR` prints the four lines `before.txt` holds, `EVAL` prints numbers no lower than its `before.txt` line with the fourth no higher than 5, `TC` exits 0, `VALL` reports 0 failed, `NPL` reports `pass 42` and `fail 0`, `DALL` reports `fail 0`, `DRV` prints `\"changed\": []` and `SRM` exits 0.\n136: - [ ] T033 [C] Check the boundaries. Verify: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --quiet HEAD -- AGENTS.md .skilled/commands/create $ADV/lib/render.ts $ADV/tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` exits 0, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff HEAD -U0 -- .skilled .opencode/plugins | rg \"^\\+.*(//|#|\\*).*(specs/|REQ-0|ADR-0|T0[0-9]{2}|[Pp]hase [0-9]|[Rr]ank [0-9])\"` prints nothing, the same pattern over `MBCT` prints nothing, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --stat HEAD -- '*package.json' '*package-lock.json'` prints nothing, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --short -- .skilled .opencode/plugins` lists only files named in this phase's tasks and `rg -l \"SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook` still lists the two playbooks that set it.\n137: - [ ] T034 [C] Write `implementation-summary.md` and mark each row in `acceptance-criteria.md` with its evidence (`implementation-summary.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md`). Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n138: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n139: \n140: ---\n141: \n142: <!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n143: ## Completion Criteria\n144: \n145: - [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n146: - [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n147: - [ ] `BASE` reads `needs_mode_floor` 1 of 35, `$SP/summary-final-after.json` prints the SC-002 line and every floor holds against `$SP/before.txt`\n148: <!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n149: \n150: ---\n151: \n152: <!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n153: ## Cross-References\n154: \n155: - **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n156: - **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n157: - **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n158: - **Research**: `../009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research-segment-3.md`\n159: <!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n160: \n161: ---\n162: \n163: ## Verification Checklist\n164: \n165: <!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n166: ## Verification Protocol\n167: \n168: | Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n169: |----------|----------|-------------------|\n170: | **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n171: | **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n172: | **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n173: \n174: A blocked task gets `[B]` and one line naming what blocks it. A moved floor blocks the phase.\n175: <!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n176: \n177: ---\n178: \n179: <!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n180: ## Pre-Implementation\n181: \n182: - [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Phase 014 is committed and its shared files are listed before wave 1 (T001). Evidence: `$SP/phase-014-files.txt`.\n183: - [ ] CHK-002 [P0] The before numbers are in `scratch/before.txt` and match `spec.md` section 2 (T002). Evidence: the T002 verify lines.\n184: <!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n185: \n186: ---\n187: \n188: <!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n189: ## Code Quality\n190: \n191: - [ ] CHK-010 [P0] `TC` exits 0 and `node --check` passes on `CAP`, `MBC`, `S`, `OF`, `R` and `PLG`. Evidence: `TC` in `$SP/after.txt` and the six `node --check` exits.\n192: - [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No added code comment names a spec path, a phase number, a task id or a rank id (T033). Evidence: the T033 label scans print nothing.\n193: - [ ] CHK-012 [P0] `unsafe` is computed as before. Evidence: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -U0 HEAD -- $S | rg \"^[-+].*unsafe: start.unsafe\"` prints nothing.\n194: - [ ] CHK-013 [P1] The default record is prompt-free and drops the skill label and the error text (T012, T026). Evidence: the `STT` case and the T026 tail line.\n195: <!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n196: \n197: ---\n198: \n199: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n200: ## Testing Checklist\n201: \n202: - [ ] CHK-020 [P0] Every floor holds (T032). Evidence: `$SP/after.txt` beside `$SP/before.txt`.\n203: - [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The recaptured baseline reads `needs_mode_floor` 1 of 35 and one label row (T024). Evidence: the T024 `jq` lines.\n204: - [ ] CHK-022 [P0] The final arm prints the SC-002 line (T031). Evidence: `$SP/summary-final-after.json`.\n205: - [ ] CHK-023 [P0] 301 default writes leave 200 lines (T012). Evidence: the `STT` trim case.\n206: - [ ] CHK-024 [P1] The live heads and the render probe read as SC-004 says (T027, T028). Evidence: `$SP/live-heads.txt` and `$SP/render-entries-after.json`.\n207: - [ ] CHK-025 [P1] The brief-cost test passes and one live run is recorded (T005, T030). Evidence: `V tests/measure-brief-cost.vitest.ts` and `$SP/brief-cost-live.json`.\n208: - [ ] CHK-026 [P1] The DSH session choice names the one session the prompt opened (T029). Evidence: `$SP/dsh-session.txt`.\n209: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n210: \n211: ---\n212: \n213: <!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n214: ## FIX ADDENDUM: FIX COMPLETENESS\n215: \n216: - [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Each item has a class: health default `cross-consumer` (six writers, three readers), degraded flag `cross-consumer`, needs-mode label `class-of-bug` (every deferring hub), top-only guard `instance-only`, OpenCode line `instance-only`, brief cost `instance-only`, `deliveryUnknown` `instance-only`, DSH session id `instance-only` and `unsafeNoChangedPath` `matrix/evidence`. Evidence: the classes match the affected surfaces in `plan.md`.\n217: - [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producers: `rg -n \"requireDebug\" $ADV/lib` lists the two sink callers and only the diagnostic one changed. Evidence: the `rg` output.\n218: - [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Every consumer of a changed field is in the `plan.md` addendum. Evidence: the consumer `rg` in `plan.md` lists no file outside the addendum.\n219: - [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P1] The record subset is a field drop, not a parser change: the `STT` case persists a record that held both fields and reads neither back, and `rejects diagnostic records with forbidden fields` in `tests/legacy/advisor-observability.vitest.ts` still passes. Evidence: both cases in T012's verify.\n220: - [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] The matrix axes in `plan.md` each have a case in T012, T014, T020 or T026. Evidence: the case names.\n221: - [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] The cases that read `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` delete and restore it, and `VALL` runs with `AI_SESSION_CHILD` unset. Evidence: the `STT` cases and the T032 command.\n222: - [ ] CHK-FIX-007 [P1] Evidence names the commit it ran on. Evidence: `$SP/after.txt` and `implementation-summary.md` name it.\n223: <!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n224: \n225: ---\n226: \n227: <!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n228: ## Security\n229: \n230: - [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No task prints holdout prompt text. Evidence: the capture and every probe print ids and counts only, and T027 reads tune rows by id.\n231: - [ ] CHK-031 [P0] No task starts a model session or ollama, and no task writes under the home folder. Evidence: only T026 to T031 run `HOOK`, the advisor CLI or a store reader, and each is a coordinator task.\n232: - [ ] CHK-032 [P1] The default record file stays private. Evidence: `V tests/metrics-file-permissions.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed in T012.\n233: <!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n234: \n235: ---\n236: \n237: <!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n238: ## Documentation\n239: \n240: - [ ] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` state the same numbers. Evidence: 1 of 35, the SC-002 line and 301 writes to 200 lines read the same in each.\n241: - [ ] CHK-041 [P1] The five documents and the advisor leg match the code (T007 to T011, T017, T025). Evidence: their verify commands print what they say.\n242: <!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n243: \n244: ---\n245: \n246: <!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n247: ## File Organization\n248: \n249: - [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Every measurement lives in `scratch/` and no probe script is left in the tree. Evidence: `ls scratch` lists the files the tasks name.\n250: - [ ] CHK-051 [P1] No file outside the tasks' list changed (T033). Evidence: the T033 status line.\n251: <!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n252: \n253: ---\n254: \n255: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n256: ## Verification Summary\n257: \n258: | Category | Total | Verified |\n259: |----------|-------|----------|\n260: | P0 Items | 14 | 0/14 |\n261: | P1 Items | 13 | 0/13 |\n262: | P2 Items | 0 | 0/0 |\n263: \n264: **Verification Date**: 2026-11-13\n265: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/015-health-default-and-brief-refinements/tasks.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794565827319,"end":1794565827920}}}}
